            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-102473",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "dash: dash: Super-polynomial backtracking in pmatch when libc fnmatch is disabled"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in dash. When built without libc fnmatch, the internal pmatch() matcher implements * by unbounded recursion over candidate positions. A local user who can plant filenames, or otherwise feed that matcher, can make a short multi-star pattern such as *.*.*.*.*.tar.gz consume excessive CPU."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-102473",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-102473\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: dash\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-102473](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-102473)\nA flaw was found in dash. When built without libc fnmatch, the internal pmatch() matcher implements * by unbounded recursion over candidate positions. A local user who can plant filenames, or otherwise feed that matcher, can make a short multi-star pattern such as *.*.*.*.*.tar.gz consume excessive CPU.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-102473**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|dash||[CVE-2026-102473](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-102473)|\n\nA flaw was found in dash. When built without libc fnmatch, the internal pmatch() matcher implements * by unbounded recursion over candidate positions. A local user who can plant filenames, or otherwise feed that matcher, can make a short multi-star pattern such as *.*.*.*.*.tar.gz consume excessive CPU."
